# Trudy Backend & Frontend Integration Plan (Single-Agency, Client-Scoped)

## Goals
- Clean contracts between Next.js frontend and FastAPI backend.
- Type-safe client, resilient uploads, realtime updates.

## API contract
- Single OpenAPI v3.1 spec (`docs/api/reference/openapi.yaml`).
- Generate TS types; Pydantic models on backend.
- Request correlation: `X-Request-Id`; tenancy scoping via `x-client-id` header (validated against JWT claim) and enforced by RLS in Supabase.

## Auth & session
- Auth0 for login (frontend). Backend validates JWT (RS256) and extracts `sub`, `role`, optional `client_id`.
- Frontend includes bearer token + `x-client-id` for client-scoped operations.

## Data fetching
- React Query keys: ['agents', clientId], ['voices', clientId], ['kb', id], ['campaigns', id], ['calls', id].
- Background revalidation; normalized errors.

## Uploads
- Flow: FE requests presign → uploads to S3 → FE posts ingest → BE validates → triggers Ultravox actions.
- Multipart + resume for large files.

## Realtime updates
- SSE/WebSocket channel per client for events: voice.training.*, campaign.*, call.*
- Fallback polling.

## Local cache & drafts
- IndexedDB for drafts and upload queue; namespaced by clientId.

## Error handling
- Unified error envelope; idempotent GET retries only.

## Observability
- Propagate `request_id` and `client_id` to Sentry on both FE/BE.

## Milestones
- Types from OpenAPI → TS types.
- API client wrapper (auth, retries, correlation id, x-client-id).
- Presigned upload flow (KB + voice samples).
- Realtime events wired to UI components.

## Acceptance criteria
- FE builds against generated types.
- Reliable uploads with resume and verified callbacks.
- Live status updates without manual refresh for voice training and campaigns.


